#: be500659dc1d4521b75de991172fe72d
msgid "**Who should read this page?**"
msgstr "**このページを読むべき方**:"

#: ../../explanation/validated_algorithms.md:11
#: 486ffb0b5cd74cf6beb9ff2e4c47d86d
msgid ""
"Researchers who want to verify the mathematical and physical validity of the"
" methods."
msgstr "解析手法の数学的・物理学的な妥当性を確認したい研究者"

#: ../../explanation/validated_algorithms.md:12
#: fac689d7b09746bfb480bb3eb33638ab
msgid ""
"Developers who need to know the numerical tolerances between GWexpy and "
"external libraries (SciPy, LALSuite, etc.)."
msgstr "外部ライブラリ（SciPy, LALSuite 等）と GWexpy の数値的な計算誤差を知りたい開発者"

#: ../../explanation/validated_algorithms.md:13
#: 81333ec478d9482d8bafdbb895a6280b
msgid ""
"Users who need to check the data characteristics (stationarity, Gaussianity,"
" etc.) assumed by each algorithm."
msgstr "使用するアルゴリズムが前提としているデータ特性（定常性、ガウス性など）を確認したい方"

#: ../../explanation/validated_algorithms.md:17
#: ea2cb9e955864b10b654ae716e48d1b1
msgid "**Advanced validation/theory companion**"
msgstr "**高度な検証・理論ページです**"

#: ../../explanation/validated_algorithms.md:19
#: c40080f8e05b4ace8ce8f53482eaae1a
msgid ""
"This page intentionally stays under the user guide so readers can discover "
"it from feature docs, but it is not an onboarding page. Treat it as the "
"advanced/theory landing for audit-oriented reading across the API reference,"
" theory notes, and targeted tutorials. For first-use guidance, start with "
"[Getting Started](../tutorials/getting_started.md), [Prerequisites and "
"Conventions](prerequisites_and_conventions.md), or the linked tutorials for "
"each method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../explanation/validated_algorithms.md:22
#: 0209c270bfef45c2b69d2a8bbdd79c45
msgid ""
"The numerical algorithms implemented in `gwexpy` have undergone a rigorous "
"validation process to ensure scientific accuracy and reliability."
msgstr "`gwexpy` で使用されている主要な数値アルゴリズムは、科学的な正確性を保証するために厳密な検証プロセスを経て実装されています。"

#: ../../explanation/validated_algorithms.md:25
#: 1ffacfa46e83451e8036ab647c4db82a
msgid "Validation Criteria and Numerical Precision"
msgstr "検証の基準と計算精度 (Validation & Precision)"

#: ../../explanation/validated_algorithms.md:27
#: 52cc1440ca3249679a829674157f9a9d
msgid ""
"Algorithms labeled as \"Validated\" meet the following standards and achieve"
" specific precision (tolerance) benchmarks:"
msgstr "「検証済み」と表記されるアルゴリズムは、以下の基準に基づき、指定の精度（Tolerance）を達成しています。"

#: ../../explanation/validated_algorithms.md:29
#: cd545f785dea421194107e4be3350b1f
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Tolerance**: We generally use $10^{-12}$ (relative error) as the passing "
"criterion. This indicates no significant logic differences beyond standard "
"double-precision rounding errors."
msgstr ""
"**一致率 (Tolerance)**: $10^{-12}$ (相対誤差) "
"を原則的なパス基準としています。これは倍精度浮動小数点演算において、丸め誤差以外の有意なロジック差異がないことを示します。"

#: ../../explanation/validated_algorithms.md:30
#: 980a895a24eb4d7a9d59cb93a623948e
msgid ""
"**Invariance**: All algorithms are verified for \"Scale Invariance,\" "
"ensuring results remain consistent even after scaling data (e.g., "
"multiplying by 1000)."
msgstr ""
"**物理的不変性 (Invariance)**: スケール変換（データの 1000 倍など）をしても結果が整合する「Scale "
"Invariance」を全アルゴリズムで検証しています。"

